{"id":"D","text":"does measures"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The missing person is the **subject**, not the object.","explanation":"**Who** is the subject, so use the singular present form **measures** without an extra do.","keywords":["subject-question"],"skill":"subject-question","contextKey":"question-forms-3","fingerprint":"f200f1b79409dd15e665527eaca2bd69430c5de6ca5ce96e6a0f904399c721bc","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-question-forms"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The missing person is the **subject**, not the object.","**Who** is the subject, so use the singular present form **measures** without an extra do.","Choose **measures**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Is cannot take this base action verb in a neutral present-simple question.","B":"A to-infinitive is not a finite predicate after who.","C":"**Who** is the subject, so use the singular present form **measures** without an extra do.","D":"This marks the main verb as well as adding does; the form after does would have to be base."}}},{"id":"8119dc83-6cbf-527c-afba-ef5066649b41","topicSlug":"question-forms","level":"A1","prompt":"“Did they measure the garden fence yesterday?” Complete the positive short answer: “Yes, they ____.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"were"},{"id":"B","text":"have"},{"id":"C","text":"did"},{"id":"D","text":"do"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Match the short answer’s auxiliary to the question.","explanation":"Repeat **did**, the auxiliary from the past-simple question.","keywords":["matching-short-answer"],"skill":"matching-short-answer","contextKey":"question-forms-3","fingerprint":"d5ee6c3fafdceb0c550b9bcb8d6ce860cc1af495e9528ee9849e139133a49761","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-question-forms"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewSta