akes **does**; translate stays in the base form."}}},{"id":"f94f4458-d9c8-558b-a3db-43d2e682b62e","topicSlug":"question-forms","level":"A1","prompt":"Complete the past-simple question: “Why did the assistant ____ the travel leaflet?”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"translate"},{"id":"B","text":"translates"},{"id":"C","text":"to translate"},{"id":"D","text":"been translate"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The past marker is already on **did**; do not mark it twice.","explanation":"**Did** carries the past tense, so choose base **translate**.","keywords":["past-question-base"],"skill":"past-question-base","contextKey":"question-forms-4","fingerprint":"75a598e8a4edaece8c75bd33972bd6b8752cbadc829a9d5ebc226b1491ea86fa","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-question-forms"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The past marker is already on **did**; do not mark it twice.","**Did** carries the past tense, so choose base **translate**.","Choose **translate**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"**Did** carries the past tense, so choose base **translate**.","B":"The third-person -s form cannot follow did in this question.","C":"Did takes a bare infinitive, without to.","D":"Been cannot follow did to build this question."}}},{"id":"3aad342a-7b5e-5bef-a2e8-391191dc4787","topicSlug":"question-forms","level":"A1","prompt":"Ask who performs the action, in the neutral present simple: “Who ____ the travel leaflet each morning?”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"is translate"},{"id":"B","text":"to translate"},{"id":"C","text":"translates"},{"id":"D","text":"does translates"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The missing person is the **subject**, not the object.","explanation":"**Who** is the subject, so use the singular present form **translates** without an extra do.","keywords":["subject-question"],"skill":"subject